{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>From beyond the rivers of Cush, My suppliants, [even] the daughter of My dispersed, [shall bring] My offering.</b> Thus [it is with] \"the daughter of My dispersed (בַּת־פוּצַי)\" — and the vav is missing, like שֶׁמֶשׁ יָרֵחַ. Therefore he said: יוֹבִילוּן מִנְחָתִי (\"they shall bring My offering\") — both of them. And some say: כִּי עֲתָרַי יִשְׂרָאֵל — they are Israel, who pray (עוֹתָרִים) to HaShem, and they are dispersed among the nations — יוֹבִילוּן מִנְחָה (\"they shall bring an offering\") to HaShem."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's Hebrew quotes the phrase שם גוי at the head, apparently referencing the preceding words מֵעֵבֶר לְנַהֲרֵי כוּש (\"from beyond the rivers of Cush\"); translated hyper-literally as it stands. The phrase שמש ירח likely illustrates a construct pair without intervening vav."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:33.264093361Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}